PanVK CSF: give compute jobs the shared TLS size, not their own stack size

Command buffers use one TLS allocation, sized for the largest stack of any
shader in them. A compute (or precomp, or GPU-prerast) job copies the shared
descriptor's base pointer into its private TSD but left the TSD's TLS size
word set to the job's own shader stack size. With packed TLS addressing --
the default on Valhall v9 and later, so G615/G715 included -- the thread
stack stride is derived from that size word. When jobs with different stack
sizes run without an intervening barrier, the job with the smaller stride
writes its stacks on top of the other job's, corrupting TLS.

DXVK runs many small compute jobs (Unity's auto exposure and bloom among
them) back to back, so it hits this on essentially every frame. The corrupt
exposure reads back as NaN/Inf, tonemaps to white, and the temporal history
then keeps the frame white.

Copy word 0 (TLS size) of the shared descriptor along with the base pointer
at all three CSF sites that dispatch a compute-style job.

Ported from upstream Mesa 81db71cf ("panvk/csf: give compute jobs the TLS
size of the shared allocation"), which fixes the same class of GPU page
fault on Mali-G615. The third site is DroidDeck's own GPU-prerast launcher,
which copies the same descriptor and needs the same fix.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c
index 3586e17..5985d99 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c
@@ -410,11 +410,13 @@ cmd_dispatch(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf, struct panvk_dispatch_info *info)
 
    struct cs_builder *b = panvk_get_cs_builder(cmdbuf, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_COMPUTE);
 
-   /* Copy the global TLS pointer to the per-job TSD. */
+   /* Copy the global TLS pointer and size to the per-job TSD. */
    if (cs->info.tls_size) {
       cs_move64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), cmdbuf->state.tls.desc.gpu);
+      cs_load32_to(b, cs_scratch_reg32(b, 4), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 0);
       cs_load64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 2), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 8);
       cs_move64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), tsd);
+      cs_store32(b, cs_scratch_reg32(b, 4), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 0);
       cs_store64(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 2), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 8);
       cs_flush_stores(b);
    }
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 1733fa3..bf780b4 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -3737,15 +3737,19 @@ gpu_prerast_launch_cs_desc(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
                            uint64_t push_uniforms, uint64_t tsd,
                            const struct panvk_dispatch_info *info)
 {
-   /* Same TLS pointer copy as cmd_dispatch(): the global TLS descriptor is
-    * only filled at EndCommandBuffer, so copy its pointer on the GPU.
+   /* Same TLS pointer and size copy as cmd_dispatch(): the global TLS
+    * descriptor is only filled at EndCommandBuffer, so copy both words on the
+    * GPU. The size word sets the thread-stack stride, so a stale value here
+    * corrupts the shared stack allocation.
     */
    if (cs->info.tls_size) {
       struct cs_builder *b =
          panvk_get_cs_builder(cmdbuf, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_COMPUTE);
       cs_move64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), cmdbuf->state.tls.desc.gpu);
+      cs_load32_to(b, cs_scratch_reg32(b, 4), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 0);
       cs_load64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 2), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 8);
       cs_move64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), tsd);
+      cs_store32(b, cs_scratch_reg32(b, 4), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 0);
       cs_store64(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 2), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 8);
       cs_flush_stores(b);
    }
